      "message": "This pointer is set up by pKVM in `__pkvm__enable_virtualization_cpu` hypercall, which is called by the host in kvm_init() -\u003e kvm_init_virtualization() -\u003e kvm_enable_virtualization() -\u003e kvm_enable_virtualization_cpu() -\u003e kvm_arch_enable_virtualization_cpu() -\u003e pkvm_enable_virtualization_cpu(), which happens _later_ than vmx_pkvm_init() returns, i.e. in particular, later than IOMMU driver initialization?\n\nSo if we want to use it for IOMMU hypercalls, we should initialize it much earlier, probably in __pkvm_init_finalise()?\n\n(Looks like you are not actually using it for IOMMU hypercalls in this series yet?)\n\nBesides that, if KVM\u0027s param `enable_virt_at_load` is set to false, it is initialized even later, when creating the first VM.",
